NAME
    vibeeyes - a pair of eyes that follow the pointer

SYNOPSIS
    vibeeyes

DESCRIPTION
    A window with two eyes whose pupils follow the mouse pointer, the
    old xeyes joke. As the pointer moves, the kernel hands the window
    the pixel under it and the pupils turn to look at it. When the
    pointer is over the desktop rather than over a window, the focused
    window still hears where it is, so the eyes keep tracking after the
    cursor has left their window; a position past the edge is still a
    direction to look in.

    The eyes blink now and then, on the one-second heartbeat every
    windowed program is given.

KEYS
    Esc   close the window
